      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this necessary? oti502_get_val takes a pointer to a signed integer, so it seems like it would be worthwhile to return the actual temperature instead of cutting it off at zero. Many batteries have a minimum operating temperature below 0 (usually -20 or -10 C), so if the temperature is -30 C, where the battery is outside its operating temperature, and we report 0, the system will continue to run, possibly damaging the battery.",
      "revId": "79f245d505f0c5cd24663fbdcfbfa9cd3456c073",
